  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A horizontal force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;is applied at the centre of mass of a cylindrical object of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, perpendicular to its axis as shown in the figure. The coefficient of friction between the object and the ground is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi></math>. The centre of mass of the object has an acceleration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>. The acceleration due to gravity is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math>. Given that the object rolls without slipping, which of the following statement(s) is (are) correct?</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/c40aaf47-970f-42c6-a45c-5b3be0c39e9a-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 177px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "qtNwl",
      "text": "For the same&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;does not depend on whether the cylinder is solid or hollow.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ckbai",
      "text": "For a solid cylinder, the maximum possible value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Bx8g7",
      "text": "The magnitude of the frictional force on the object due to the ground is always&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vKlZ8",
      "text": "For a thin-walled hollow cylinder,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let moment of inertia&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/f4eb0c6e-932c-407c-b3e4-d033856c2fa9-758f5244-8b39-44c0-b24d-ebcc14e0b238-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 256px;\" /></p><p>For pure rolling,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>I</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>I</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>I</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;For the same value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>, value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> depends on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;For a solid cylinder<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;(to calculate maximum&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is dependent on applied force.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;For thin-walled hollow cylinder<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p>",
